ntial/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5t+3{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15t+5{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-98689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,q(t)=4{t}^{2}-t-1\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}-2t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-98689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=2{t}^{2}-2t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{-1}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{0}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+{p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{0}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+t)={t}^{2}+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2t+({t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-98689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5b230d17b7baeef6583e5d2bd3fabe574eda2e1743d3405d807e7717e8a758c"} {"question" "q-98689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-98689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{t}^{2}+t"] ["math" "3{t}^{2}-t"] ["math" "{t}^{2}+2t"] ["math" "{t}^{2}-2t"] ["math" "{t}^{2}-3t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-98689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{t}^{2}-t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=1,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,g(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}$ equals $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(t){f}_{1}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+3t]_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(2-0+3\\pi )-(2-0-3\\pi ) \\\\  & =6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t) & =\\frac{6\\pi }{2\\pi }\\cdot 1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5b230d17b7baeef6583e5d2bd3fabe574eda2e1743d3405d807e7717e8a758c"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] ["math" "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "6+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-1,1]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$ \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)={t}^{2},\\,g(t)=15t+3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}$ equals $15t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=15t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(15t+3)\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{15}{4}{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4}+1)-(\\frac{15}{4}-1) \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{f}_{2}(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{2}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{5}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-(-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{2}{(\\frac{2}{5})}\\cdot {t}^{2}=5{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =15t+5{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5b230d17b7baeef6583e5d2bd3fabe574eda2e1743d3405d807e7717e8a758c"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15t+3{t}^{2}"] ["math" "15t+5{t}^{2}"] ["math" "3t+5{t}^{2}"] ["math" "3{t}^{2}"] ["math" "5t+3{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15t+5{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(3t+2)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-5‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩ & =(5t-5){|}_{0}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{0}+(5t-5){|}_{1}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{25}=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5b230d17b7baeef6583e5d2bd3fabe574eda2e1743d3405d807e7717e8a758c"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(2t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖6t-2‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-24t+4)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-12+4)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{4}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073079/state.json" "file_sha256" "61ec4b0745f79ca26bef97f84fbb31857dd0b2bf81c12aa81ab0ed5588866cbc"} {"question" "q-105498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :questi